                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ladra is a short, but solid experience. You'll spend your time between stealth missions and chatting with a few NPCs.\r\nStealth works considerably well since we're talking about RPG Maker. Other than the fact that sometimes I got away with things I wouldn't expect to, the mechanics introduced worked well. Solving each level wasn't that complex and sometimes you could force/rush through some parts, but overall delivers what it proposes.\r\nThe small dialogue bits are actually great, I'd say. Even the glimpses we got are better worldbuilding and well crafted dialogues than many more elaborated allegedly \"story\" games xD There is enough dialogue to put you on Estella shoes and why she's doing it, also getting smalls bits of world, characters and events info.\r\n\r\nI'd say you can look for up to 2 hours of playtime if you plan on doing all achievements, a bit less than one hour if you don't. For the price it is, it might be worth your time.  (15 Brazilian Reais for me)",
